{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":2,"output":3,"cacheRead":38435,"cacheWrite":781,"totalTokens":39221,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.0000015,"cacheRead":0.00038435,"cacheWrite":0.000097625,"total":0.000483675,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Both parts of the bug are fixed in `rich/table.py` and `rich/_ratio.py`.\n\n**Collapse of flexible columns**\n- `Table._calculate_column_widths` now computes a per-column minimum for flexible columns: one content character plus padding (`(column.width or 1) + padding`).\n- `_collapse_widths` takes an optional `minimum_widths` argument and won't shrink a column below its minimum. The \"last resort\" even reduction also respects those minimums.\n- The repro now renders `Load` and `82%`. At `width=45` and below, `Load` shows as `…` instead of disappearing into `||`.\n\n**Degenerate ratio inputs**\n- `ratio_distribute`: the `assert total_ratio > 0` is gone. Empty ratio lists return `[]`, all-zero ratios fall back to even distribution, and a negative total is treated as zero so each slot gets only its minimum.\n- `ratio_resolve`: a zero-denominator guard returns minimum sizes instead of raising `ZeroDivisionError`.\n\n**Verification**\n- Empty tables with `expand=True`, zero ratios, and `min_width` all render without exceptions.\n- The full test suite shows the same 12 failures before and after my change (in `test_syntax`, `test_markdown`, `test_card`). These are pre-existing and unrelated to tables or ratios. The 939 passing tests include `test_ratio.py`, `test_tools.py`, and `test_table.py`.\n\nI didn't run `black` because it isn't installed in this environment."}}
